(GRM-09: args ::= arg_clause ("and" arg_clause)*, arg_clause ::= loop_expansion
 | expr - a call's arguments can each independently be either a plain
 value or a loop_expansion (a grid call: one call per combination of the
 expanded arguments). Cross-ref LST2-44 (collections-b.md), whose note on
 "gen call grid" already establishes this pattern is generator-emitted
 elsewhere; this is the Grammar Summary's own minimal two-argument grid
 witness (bare statement call, so nothing is printed - the claim under
 test is that it PARSES and RUNS to completion without error, not what
 it prints).
